o3y|v|To draw off by degrees; to cause to flow gradually out or off; hence, to cause the exhaustion of. ; To exhaust of liquid contents by drawing them off; to make gradually dry or empty; to remove surface water, as from streets, by gutters, etc.; to deprive of moisture; hence, to exhaust; to empty of wealth, resources, or the like; as, to drain a country of its specie. ; To filter. ; To flow gradually; as, the water of low ground drains off. ; To become emptied of liquor by flowing or dropping; as, let the vessel stand and drain.	o:765,50,21;tjz,45,5;16x4,1,2~765,50,21;tjz,45,5;16x4,1,2	s:765,26,4~765,26,4	d:1co4,90,2;765,40,11;wbb,34,5~765,40,11;wbb,34,5;1co4,90,2	D:tjz,42,4;765,37,9;29qk,19,10;1fiq,1,5~29qk,19,10;765,37,9;1fiq,1,5;tjz,42,4
