o4c|n|A composition, in prose or poetry, accommodated to action, and intended to exhibit a picture of human life, or to depict a series of grave or humorous actions of more than ordinary interest, tending toward some striking result. It is commonly designed to be spoken and represented by actors on the stage. ; A series of real events invested with a dramatic unity and interest. ; Dramatic composition and the literature pertaining to or illustrating it; dramatic literature.	a:2h12,62,1;1fiq,36,12;22gw,5,4~1fiq,36,12;22gw,5,4;2h12,62,1	v:c9p,55,5~c9p,55,5	n:2h12,62,1;2gt7,19,3~2gt7,19,3;2h12,62,1	N:1syf,89,1~1syf,89,1
