o9n|n|Liquid to be swallowed; any fluid to be taken into the stomach for quenching thirst or for other purposes, as water, coffee, or decoctions. ; Specifically, intoxicating liquor; as, when drink is on, wit is out.	a:22a1,53,2;11o1,52,4~11o1,52,4;22a1,53,2	n:qgh,67,8~qgh,67,8	N:est,50,1~est,50,1
o9n|v|To swallow anything liquid, for quenching thirst or other purpose; to imbibe; to receive or partake of, as if in satisfaction of thirst; as, to drink from a spring. ; To quaff exhilarating or intoxicating liquors, in merriment or feasting; to carouse; to revel; hence, to lake alcoholic liquors to excess; to be intemperate in the /se of intoxicating or spirituous liquors; to tipple. ; To swallow (a liquid); to receive, as a fluid, into the stomach; to imbibe; as, to drink milk or water. ; To take in (a liquid), in any manner; to suck up; to absorb; to imbibe. ; To take in; to receive within one, through the senses; to inhale; to hear; to see. ; To smoke, as tobacco.	o:7gw,106,12;aym,97,2;est,96,24;24x,94,8;27ty,84,2;2fuf,63,4;qgh,63,6;42j,27,5~est,96,24;7gw,106,12;24x,94,8;qgh,63,6;42j,27,5;2fuf,63,4;aym,97,2;27ty,84,2	s:fq,44,4;qgh,37,1;1mfp,20,10~1mfp,20,10;fq,44,4;qgh,37,1
